#  Line endings, settled once.
#
#  This repository stores text as LF, and did so before this file existed -
#  nothing was enforcing it, which is the problem. `core.autocrlf=true` is set
#  on the machine this was built on, so a clone checks out CRLF; any tool that
#  then writes \n turns a two-sentence edit into a whole-file diff. That
#  already happened once in the parent working repository, where a two-number
#  correction to IMPLEMENTATION.md showed as 748 changed lines.
#
#  `text=auto eol=lf` fixes the stored form as LF regardless of what the
#  working tree holds, so a diff shows only what actually changed.
#
#  (Checked, not assumed: the blobs here were already LF. `git show HEAD:<f>`
#  appeared to print CRLF, but that is autocrlf smudging the OUTPUT - the blob
#  OIDs are unchanged by `git add --renormalize`, which is the real test.)
* text=auto eol=lf

#  Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
